mes a relevant change, the memo does not give up at once. The edit index of the sealed sidecar maps every entry to the rows that name it and every directory to the rows that read its children; the lookup re-checks exactly those rows with the planner's own checks (an analysis is replayed and compared by its result, so an edit that keeps a file's imports and modules holds), proves a directory that has relevant entries below it to be the same directory (frontier inode), lists a frontier directory whose children changed again with the planner's own walk predicates and compares its subdirectories and members, refuses a touched path that became a symbolic link, a row it cannot check (a derived fact, a closure) and more than `maximumEditPaths` paths or `maximumEditRows` rows; when everything holds it serves and re-seals the stamps of the directories it listed again. Derived refinement: a re-checked row that does not hold and that only pseudo owners hold (the support of derived facts), and a derived fact the journal names, make the memo ask those questions again with the planner's own derivation (`openGenerationDeriverV1`, `settleSuspectsV1`) in a child process of the same invocation (`Policy.derive`); it serves only when every answer is the recorded one and every new support reads only entries the old support read; a stale row a project or the environment holds itself, a failed or changed answer, a new entry and more than `maximumDerivedQuestions` questions plan.",
